<title>INDIA: India Procter falls 10 percent at BSE.</title>
<headline>India Procter falls 10 percent at BSE.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Procter &amp; Gamble India lost 64.25 rupees, or 10.0 percent, to 578.50 rupees at the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) on Friday after the firm announced poor six-month results, dealers said.  </p>
<p>The company on Friday said its six-month net profit ending December 1996 dropped 6.1 percent to 142.5 million rupees against 151.7 million rupees in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>It's net sales rose 20 percent to 2.05 billion rupees in 1996 from 1.71 billion the previous year.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-2-265 9000</p>
